@@ -153,6 +153,32 @@ The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
       Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
       the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional alias expression is supplied with the
+   ``canonical`` option and is displayed after an equals sign. Its type names
+   are parsed as Python annotations and can be cross-referenced. For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+   Type aliases may also be documented inside a class. They do not create a
+   namespace for declarations in their body.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: alias expression
+      :type: text
+
+      The expression assigned to the type alias. It is displayed in the
+      signature and parsed using the Python annotation parser.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:exception:: name[type parameters](parameters)
